// Title: Microsoft 365 detected threat delivered through an explicit allow override
// Rule name: NO-MITRE-MAPPING - Detected threat allow override delivery
// Classification: Hunting query
// Maturity: hunting
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR advanced hunting
// Telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Office 365 EmailEvents
// MITRE ATT&CK: NO-MITRE-MAPPING - the match is a mail-control outcome, not a specific attacker technique
// Purpose: Find inbound messages that received a threat verdict, matched an organization- or user-level
// allow override, and were recorded as delivered.
// Logic: Require one EmailEvents row with inbound direction, non-empty ThreatTypes, an explicit Allow value
// in OrgLevelAction or UserLevelAction, and DeliveryAction == "Delivered". No IOC, threshold, join, rarity,
// content parsing, authentication-string assumption, or inferred post-delivery outcome is used.
// Match proves: Defender recorded a threat verdict, an explicit allow override, and delivered initial action
// for the same recipient/message event.
// Match does not prove: the verdict is correct, the message remains in the inbox, authentication failed,
// a tracked brand was spoofed, the recipient opened or acted on the message, or an account was compromised.
// False positives: necessary vendor exceptions, approved simulations, test policies, or false-positive verdicts.
// Limits: Defender for Office 365 Plan 2 and populated EmailEvents fields are required; policy ownership,
// current message location, recipient interaction, and benign prevalence require local investigation.
// Validation: execute the safe isolated controls and passive prevalence review in validation.md before promotion.
// Evidence claims: C002, C003, C004, C005, C006, C007, C008, C009, C010

EmailEvents
| where EmailDirection == "Inbound"
| where ThreatTypes != ""
| where OrgLevelAction == "Allow" or UserLevelAction == "Allow"
| where DeliveryAction == "Delivered"
| project
    Timestamp,
    NetworkMessageId,
    InternetMessageId,
    SenderMailFromAddress,
    SenderFromAddress,
    SenderDisplayName,
    RecipientEmailAddress,
    Subject,
    ThreatTypes,
    ThreatNames,
    DetectionMethods,
    ConfidenceLevel,
    AuthenticationDetails,
    DeliveryAction,
    DeliveryLocation,
    LatestDeliveryAction,
    LatestDeliveryLocation,
    OrgLevelAction,
    OrgLevelPolicy,
    UserLevelAction,
    UserLevelPolicy,
    EmailAction,
    EmailActionPolicy,
    ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
